NOTE (S525): the §[2] "n=22 OFF" line above shows HONEST: REJECTED / wall
122.54 s -- that was the FIRST cut of the --no-scatter-fold toggle, which
wrongly fell through to the _dt(q)=uint64 branch; over BIG_Q a plain uint64
np.add.at OVERFLOWS before the % q fold, so the scatter residues were wrong
and the chain correctly REJECTED (soundness working as intended). The bug
was fixed (explicit object branch, guarded by benchmark selftest 5) and the
CORRECT n=22 OFF object control is §[4]: HONEST: ACCEPTED, wall 249.18 s,
comm 146637 (== ON), peak RSS 988 MB (== ON). Use §[4], not §[2], for the
A/B. The fixed sweep is the basis for large_x_benchmark_results.md §S525.
